  "comment": "Configuration To configure netplan, save configuration files under /etc/netplan/ with a .yaml extension (e.g. /etc/netplan/config.yaml), then run sudo netplan apply. This command parses and applies the configuration to the system. Configuration written to disk under /etc/netplan/ will persist between reboots. network: version: 2 renderer: networkd ethernets: enp1s0: dhcp4: no enp2s0: dhcp4: no",
